Day 012 - Student Management

Concepts Used
* Class and objects
* Array of objects
* Methods

Requirements
1. Add student (id, name, marks)
2. View all students
3. Search by id
4. Delete by id


Class Design

class Student {
    int id;
    String name;
    double marks;
}

Starter Code

Student[] students = new Student[50];
int count = 0;
void add(Student s) { students[count++] = s; }
Student find(int id) {
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
        if (students[i].id == id) return students[i];
    return null;
}

Interview Questions
1). Why use objects instead of separate arrays for each field?
2). What happens when the array is full?

